Cell["\<\
\"StateRendering\" and \"EventRendering\" settle the question either way, and \
\"MaxDrawnVertices\" moves the line.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e31f64eb-c74d-3d45-9e52-d82d37a0e154"],

Cell["Keeping track of the options", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0b5f1013-54bb-b849-a0cf-71c0b1b96e35"],

Cell["\<\
There are enough options now that they are kept in one registry, with their \
defaults:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5c51afa7-25c9-f141-b8b3-de76ca44ef55"],

Cell["$HypergraphRewritingOptions", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e3413b83-01d4-ed49-a0f9-d650d482525b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"MaxStates\"\>", "\[Rule]", "2048"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Labeled\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"LabelPatterns\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"DistinctVertices\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"CausalDependence\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Elements\"\>"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"TransitiveReduction\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"CanonicalizeStates\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"StateRendering\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Automatic"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"EventRendering\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Automatic"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"MaxDrawnVertices\"\>", "\[Rule]", "24"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"PanelSize\"\>", "\[Rule]", "90"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"HypergraphPlotOptions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"36aab2ed-52fe-\
8945-8bbf-4125ecc1714d"],

Cell["\<\
Every graph-valued property takes those together with the options of Graph, \
so ImageSize, VertexSize, GraphLayout and the rest all work. A system can \
also hold the options that describe it, rather than having them retyped on \
every call:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbd05cc6-799c-3e42-b553-b03570b79e34"],

Cell["\<\
strict = HypergraphRewritingSystem[subdivide, Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}],
  \"CausalDependence\" -> \"Edges\", \"PanelSize\" -> 70];
{Length @ strict[\"CausalEdges\", 2],
  Length @ strict[\"CausalEdges\", 2, \"CausalDependence\" -> \"Elements\"]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"68f019dd-d05a-6449-8a60-e07a8607d7b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"4", ",", "6"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"729e8a9e-bb25-7d49-8c6f-076daaa3b9d1"],

Cell["\<\
The held option is used without being repeated, and an option given to a \
property still wins over it. What is in force for a particular system:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51e9d742-5579-3643-abe0-97e03686fcfd"],

Cell["\<\
FilterRules[strict[\"Options\"], {\"CausalDependence\", \"PanelSize\", \
\"MaxDrawnVertices\"}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b4f1c2e7-e4b6-9b47-855b-d05d5b9027c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"CausalDependence\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Edges\"\>"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"MaxDrawnVertices\"\>", "\[Rule]", "24"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"PanelSize\"\>", "\[Rule]", "70"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",Expressi\
onUUID->"c0bc9cdc-b833-294b-b7ea-0cc6910228f8"],

Cell["8. Scope and limits", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"73dbf2d7-e365-934d-92c1-31a1aca71068"],

Cell["\<\
The evolution is exhaustive: every rule in every way it fits, on every state \
reached. That is what a multiway system is, and it is also how it gets \
expensive. The number of states can grow faster than expected, so \"MaxStates\
\" \[LongDash] 2048 by default \[LongDash] stops the run and says so rather \
than going on.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4d5fea46-45d0-9246-b53a-7c007ed2d213"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "A rule holds the symbols it was written with, including the ones serving as \
label variables. Giving one of those symbols a value later turns every copy \
of the rule into whatever the value is, and an expression holding itself is \
not a pleasant thing to evaluate. Keeping the variables of a rule clear of \
assignments is not a style preference here; x = something after the fact will \
break rules written months earlier."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"814ecf11-a2dc-9040-85dc-cd80ad1be97e"],

Cell["\<\
What is not here: the branchial structure beyond a single generation, causal \
invariance as a test rather than something to look at, and the token-event \
graph in the form the Multicomputation paclet gives it. Those are all built \
out of what is above and none of them needs a new idea.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dbabedd3-d69e-884a-89e9-5cacdc699e5f"],

Cell["\<\
The syntax follows the reference paclets: where they write \
MultiwaySystem[rules, init][\"CausalGraph\", n], this writes \
HypergraphRewritingSystem[rules, init][\"CausalGraph\", n], with the same \
property names. What differs is the option: their causal dependence is fixed \
at the weakest reading, and here it is chosen.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0d2896d7-55ee-6540-ac3c-5246ffe9746c"],

Cell["\<\
The file tests/CausalityExamples.wls runs the examples in this notebook as \
assertions, plus invariants checked over a hundred and twenty generated \
systems: that a causal edge always runs from an earlier generation to a later \
one, that it never reports an overlap it does not have, and that the three \
readings stand in the relation section 4 claims.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"60929cb1-f710-9b4d-952c-bcf2860203d5"],

Cell["\<\
Next: the plex diagrams that tie rewriting to hypermatrix algebra.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d18f2588-0655-2d46-a07f-0f399e682cac"]
},
